{{define "content"}}
<h1>{{.Hostname}}</h1>
<p class="sub">{{if .Rotated}}Token rotated.{{else}}Host created.{{end}}</p>

<div class="card warn">
  <p><strong>This token is shown once.</strong> It is stored only as a SHA-256
  hash, so it cannot be displayed again. If you lose it, rotate the host to
  mint a new one.{{if .Rotated}} The previous token stopped working the moment
  this one was minted.{{end}}</p>
</div>

<h2>Token</h2>
<pre>{{.Token}}</pre>

<h2>Install the agent</h2>
<p>Run this on <code>{{.Hostname}}</code>:</p>
<pre>{{.SetupCommand}}</pre>

<div class="card warn">
{{if .HubURLConfigured}}
  <p><strong>Check <code>{{.HubURL}}</code> is the address agents reach this
  hub on</strong> before running the command. It comes from
  <code>NETRA_HUB_URL</code>, and the line above pipes that host to
  <code>sh</code> and sends it this token — so a stale value hands both to
  whoever owns that name.</p>
{{else}}
  <p><strong><code>NETRA_HUB_URL</code> is not set, so the URL above is a
  placeholder.</strong> Replace both occurrences with the address agents reach
  this hub on. As written the command would pipe a stranger's script to
  <code>sh</code> and send them this token.</p>
{{end}}
</div>

<p><a href="/">← Back to hosts</a></p>
{{end}}
